fields.description:
Algorithm index. Selects the algorithm that the next start command runs.

Usage: Program before the start command; the index is checked against the algorithm built flag and the effective enable bit.

Values:
0x0 Ed25519 (reset value);
0x1 Ed25519ctx;
0x2 Ed25519ph;
0x3 Ed448;
0x4 Ed448ph;
0x5 ECDSA P-256;
0x6 ECDSA P-384;
0x7 ECDSA P-521;
0x8 ECDSA secp256k1;
0x9 ML-DSA-44;
0xA ML-DSA-65;
0xB ML-DSA-87;
0xC SLH-DSA;
0xD LMS/HSS;
0xE XMSS/XMSS^MT.

Unit: code

Limits: The code 0xF is reserved; a reserved or not built code sets the unsupported-operation error.

Operation select. Selects key generation, signing or verification for the next start command.

Usage: Program before the start command; the operation must be built for the selected algorithm.

Values:
0x0 key generation;
0x1 signing;
0x2 verification (reset value);
0x3 reserved.

Unit: code

Limits: SLH-DSA, LMS/HSS and XMSS/XMSS^MT accept only verification in this version.

Hash function select. Selects the hash function of ECDSA and of every prehash digest.

Usage: Program before the start command of ECDSA or a prehash form; the digest length must fit the curve security.

Values:
0x0 SHA-256 (reset value);
0x1 SHA-384;
0x2 SHA-512;
0x3 SHA3-256;
0x4 SHA3-384;
0x5 SHA3-512;
0x6 and 0x7 reserved.

Unit: code

Limits: A pairing of curve and hash that gives less security than the curve is rejected with the bad-length error.

Hybrid acceptance policy. Selects which signatures must be valid for the hybrid verification to accept.

Usage: Program before a hybrid start command; used only when the hybrid feature is built.

Values:
0x0 Ed25519 and ML-DSA both valid (reset value);
0x1 Ed25519 valid;
0x2 ML-DSA valid;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: code

Limits: The reserved code sets the unsupported-operation error.
